        "title": "Not your everyday experience",
        "text": "Very spiritual place even for not so spiritual ones. A great temple with amazing art and architecture. Good old saints with ashes on their bodies praying for nirvana is a pretty common sites. You absolutely would love 100s of monkies walking around alone or in families becoming too friendly (also trying to snatch your food/camera away). Behind the temple is the holy river where bodies are cremated. Thousands of devotees visit everyday. If you visit at the right time you will be able to witness the elaborate and amazing ceremony of lord shiva. A must go if you are in Kathmandu.",
