      {
        "review_id": 226219549,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r226219549-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Tourist at Pashupatinath Temple",
        "text": "I visited the temple in June 2014, and I was guided by a very interesting person. My guide, Prem, had been a street child around the temple for a couple of years, then he started to make some money as a temple tour guide. Then he was adopted by an American family who put him through school and college. Now he is a master's graduate, speaks perfect English, and understands the Western culture. He teaches English and is a tour guide (I also did the Annapurna Circuit trek with him). Back to the temple, it is a very complex and intense Hindu temple dedicated to Shiva, who governs destruction and death. Therefore the Shiva sites are dedicated to incineration and death rituals. They happen in open air, and I stayed on the bank of the river and watched the rituals for a long time. The scenery, including the cows along the river, reminded me very much of the holy Hindu city of Varanasi, my favorite place in India. But while in Varanasi you are not allowed to take pictures of the incineration rituals, here at the temple you can, from a respectful distance. You can see some of my pictures here.\n\nIf you need an outstanding guide for the temple, Kathmandu, Annapurna, or other sites in Nepal, here's Prem's info: +977-9849082363, premthapa305@hotmail.com",
