        "title": "Shiva's palace is here..",
        "text": "To enter the main shrine you must be Hindu..but still a great place to visit.. There are the cremation sites along the river and Shiva's invisible (to us) palace is on the uppermost hill... Many sadhus, Hindu holy men, stay here all year round but many more come on Shivaratri..usually celebrated in the autumn...a very sacred pilgrimage place. The area is quite large so be prepared to walk...look around as there are many sights, often in the more out of the way spots... Definitely a must visit.",
