        "title": "Impressive, definitely worth a visit",
        "text": "A bit crowded with a few annoyances, such as monkeys and begging holey men. However, it's a unique location where you may watch (albeit voyeuristic, it felt intrusive) very personal cremation ceremonies. We watched for about 15 minutes, which is enough because you see up to four cremations at once, each in a different phase.\nYou can easily walk around here and visit the temples. A personal guide is expensive ($15) and with a good tourist guide book, you'll manage perfectly on your own. I can't remember whether there is a fee for visiting the temple grounds.\nRecommended is to visit this in the late morning / early afternoon and then take the 1 mile walk around 3 pm to Boudhanath and watch the sunset there with a cold Everest on a rooftop terrace. Perfect day.",
