      {
        "review_id": 225009183,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r225009183-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Must visit",
        "text": "I have been to many temples, and Pashupatinath is among the most unusual.  You can witness the Hindu cremation rites, meet some unusual monks, and see some striking shrines.  This should be a place of great solemnity and private worship.  Unfortunately, the intrusion of commerce leaves a bitter taste in the mouth.  First, the 1000 NR entrance fee is quite steep; second, beware of getting attached to a self-appointed guide; third, you can take photos, but if you shoot people, they expect to be paid (not mourners, but priests and others).  I got a classic shot with three monks, but it cost me 2500 NR.  And touts try to sell you trinkets.\n\nAll that said, however, this is still a place you \"must see\" on a visit to Kathmandu.",
