        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r224942043-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Cremations At Edge Of Bagmati River",
        "text": "I spent over an hour observing the ritual of Hindu cremation taking place at the edge of the Bagmati River. The pyres were built with carefully placed logs in a rectangle around smoldering embers, the body placed in the center, more logs added to cover all sides. The fire is fueled with straw or smaller pieces of wood to insure a strong fire. The family attends and watches this final ritual in the life of a Hindu believer. \n\nI entered a Park and then walked about 200 yards to stand across the Bagmati from the pyres to observe the ritual. The walkway is made of concrete and extends down to the waters edge. There is no fee to observe from there.",
